acceptance:
- id: AC-126-BOUNDARY
  statement: R5 retains its elementary Grade-9 meaning, capability, ceiling and default
    eligibility; its ladder coordinate changes only from 100 to 99 to preserve strict
    prerequisite ordering, while R6 is a non-default Owner extension at 100.
  evidence_requirements:
  - test: tests/test_issue126_circular_dynamics_explorer.py::CircularDynamicsExplorerContract::test_r5_boundary_is_preserved_and_r6_is_nondefault
  - test: tests/test_grade9_default_extension_routing.py
  - test: tests/test_grade9_motion_scope.py
- id: AC-126-PHYSICS
  statement: Radial acceleration, radial Newton-II, vertical-circle top/bottom, and
    minimum-speed claims are gate-owned; flat-curve capacity reuses the canonical
    static-friction bound.
  evidence_requirements:
  - test: tests/test_issue126_circular_dynamics_explorer.py::CircularDynamicsExplorerContract::test_quantitative_relations_are_gate_owned
- id: AC-126-FALLACY
  statement: The canonical representation and explorer treat centripetal as the role
    of the net radial force, not an additional interaction.
  evidence_requirements:
  - test: tests/test_issue126_circular_dynamics_explorer.py::CircularDynamicsExplorerContract::test_no_extra_centripetal_force_arrow
- id: AC-126-EXPLORER
  statement: Explorer visualizes velocity-direction change before forces and implements
    radial/tangential axes, m-v-r scaling, flat-curve threshold, tangent cut path,
    and vertical-circle transfer; R6 has complete Core1A/Core1B self-study route coverage.
  evidence_requirements:
  - test: tests/test_issue126_circular_dynamics_explorer.py
  - test: tests/test_grade9_motion1d_vertical_gravity_agent_a_atlas.py::Grade9Motion1DVerticalGravityAgentAAtlas::test_matrix_remains_session_ready
- id: AC-126-SCOPE
  statement: The slice remains circular dynamics only and does not alter learner state,
    exit readiness, Grade-10/11 scope, or Mathematics.
  evidence_requirements:
  - oracle: PR changed-file set and focused boundary tests.
- id: AC-126-REPO
  statement: Repository guardrails pass and v31-relay validates against exact Common@1c168695f237a8bef184a9e189be80fab87d1e78.
  evidence_requirements:
  - oracle: GitHub Actions guardrails + v31-relay on exact PR head.
- id: AC-126-ROUTING
  statement: Ordinary Grade-9 routing excludes R6, while explicit Owner extension
    routing remains available.
  evidence_requirements:
  - test: tests/test_grade9_default_extension_routing.py
quality_policy:
  level: STANDARD
  independent_review: OPTIONAL
admission_policy:
  qualification: NOT_REQUIRED
  question_policy: NONE
next:
  first_action: Add the R6 Core1A/Core1B teaching route; revise only stale extension/scope
    tests to distinguish the six-rung required Grade-9 spine from non-default R6;
    regenerate manifest and rerun exact-head guardrails.
  stop_conditions:
  - Stop if any fix makes R6 default or changes R5 teaching meaning/ceiling.
  - Stop if guardrail repair requires changing learner state, Mathematics, Grade-10/11
    scope, or shared routing semantics.
  - Stop before merge without fresh checkpoint and explicit Owner MERGE authority.
